thread:
alex: Heads-up: CI started failing for the vitest edge-runner after we shipped the SDK as ESM-only. Failure in GH actions (node18) when tests try to mock the client: `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'prototype')`. Local node20 is green.

priya: that smell like ESM/CJS interop. Are tests doing `vi.mock('my-sdk', () => ({ Client: Mock }))`? If the package only exports default, that shape won't match.

alex: yep exact line. We used to rely on CJS interop where require(module).default was a thing. After ESM-only it broke in some runners.

ben: two pragmatic options: adapt tests to ESM mocking or provide a test compatibility shim. For vitest prefer `vi.stubModule` or async mocks: `vi.mock('my-sdk', async () => { const real = await vi.importActual('my-sdk'); return { default: { ...real.default, doThing: () => 'x' } } })`.

priya: also double-check vitest.config deps handling. If a transitive dependency is CJS and gets incorrectly bundled you'll get `ReferenceError: exports is not defined`. Adding `deps.inline` for that dep and forcing esbuild platform node helps. Example config snippet we used:
```ts
export default defineConfig({
 test: {
  environment: 'node',
  deps: { inline: [/^msw/, /some-cjs-lib/] },
  esbuild: { platform: 'node', target: 'node18' }
 }
})
```
This fixes a few runtime interop errors in CI.

alex: we tried deps.inline and it fixed a couple of stack traces but mock still not picked up. Also ran into `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND: node:buffer` coming from a transformed dep.

ben: node builtins missing usually means bundling platform wrong. esbuild platform node is critical. Also ensure `bundle: false` when you don't want esbuild to inline builtins.

priya: types are also an issue. Our index.d.ts still uses `export =` style so tests complain `Property 'createClient' does not exist on type 'typeof import("../dist")'`. For ESM default+named consumers, root d.ts should expose both shapes:
```ts
declare class RedwoodClient { constructor(opts?: any); }
declare const _default: RedwoodClient;
export default _default;
export { RedwoodClient };
```
That covers `import sdk from '...'` and `import { RedwoodClient } from '...'`.

alex: I built a tiny test-only rollup that outputs a CJS file under `dist-test/` and pointed the vitest job at that. It fixed CI. Not ideal long-term but quick.

ben: nice. We did something similar: an npm script `build:test:cjs` that runs in CI matrix before tests and produces a compatibility bundle. Also keep a small shim helper to make mocking straightforward:
```js
// test/helpers/compat-shim.cjs
(async () => {
  const pkg = await import('../dist/index.mjs');
  module.exports = pkg.default ?? pkg;
})();
```
Then tests `require('./test/helpers/compat-shim.cjs')` when they need CJS shape. For vitest (ESM) use dynamic import of the shim path.

priya: one more tip: prefer `vi.importActual` or `vi.stubModule` for ESM mocks rather than returning a plain object. Returning plain object can confuse module namespace shape and break prototype chains. Example pattern that avoided the prototype error:
```js
vi.mock('my-sdk', async () => {
  const real = await vi.importActual('my-sdk');
  return { default: { ...real.default, query: () => 'mocked' } };
});
```

alex: good call. We'll convert a few flaky tests to that pattern. Also adding node20 to CI matrix helped catch differences early.

build-helper: CI note: nightly matrix will now run node18 and node20 for edge-runner; added `build:test:cjs` as an optional job gated by env var `TEST_CJS=true` so we don't slow down normal PRs.

priya: I'll write a short devex doc with:
- Vitest config example (deps.inline + esbuild.platform)
- ESM mocking patterns (vi.importActual + vi.stubModule examples)
- test-only CJS shim and build:test:cjs recipe
- minimal d.ts pattern for default + named exports
- CI recommendations (node20 in matrix, optional cjs job)

ben: ping me to review the doc. I can add a snippet for jest compatibility (extensionsToTreatAsEsm + transformIgnorePatterns) too.

alex: thanks everyone, I'll open the PR with logs and a demo shim.
